    <DataNode elementId="AT5G59440-MONOMER" textLabel="thymidylate kinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q0WW55" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The |FRAME: AT5G59440 TMPK| gene of |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;| (initially named ZEU1) encodes a |FRAME: AT5G59440-MONOMER thymidylate kinase|, an enzyme that synthesizes |FRAME: TDP dTDP|, the immediate precursor for the DNA building block |FRAME: TTP dTTP|. Disruption of the gene by a T-DNA insertion resulted in early seed abortion, at the zygote stage. Expression of the gene in the mutant was able to rescue the phenotype |CITS: [18036198]|. Transcription of the gene is activated during the G1/S-phase transition of the cell cycle. The single |FRAME: AT5G59440 TMPK| gene is capable of producing two proteins by alternative splicing; the longer isoform is targeted to the mitochondria, and the shorter to the cytosol |CITS: [18036198]|. Similar N-terminal extensions of the longer isoform are also found in TMPK ESTs of maize and of white spruce, indicating that alternative splicing of TMPK maybe common in plants.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G59440-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G59440.3" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="Q0WW55" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS01331" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR10344" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q0WW55" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q0WW55" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR027417" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q0WW55" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-26841" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G59440.3" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G59440" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18036198" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G63310-MONOMER" textLabel="Nucleoside pyrophosphate kinase II, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64903" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="635" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding nucleoside diphosphate kinase 2 (AtNDK-2) was identified from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; and recombinant expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. The molecular function of catalyzing the exchange transfer of a &amp;gamma;-phosphoryl group from a nucleoside triphosphate to a nucleoside diphosphate was confirmed with purified recombinant protein and the structure and mode of action demonstrated in the crystallized protein |CITS: [15465053]|. AtNDK-2 has been shown to be involved in the phytochrome mediated growth and developmental processes by interacting with the C-terminal domain of phytochrome A (PhyA) |CITS: [15561724]|. In addition AtNDK-2 takes part in cellular redox regulation by interacting with activated mitogen-activated protein kinases (MAPKs) conferring tolerance to environmental stresses such as reactive oxygen species (ROS) accumulation |CITS: [12506203]|. Furthermore, AtNDK-2 has been reported to be involved in auxin-regulated processes, particularly through the mediation of polar auxin transport |CITS: [15927941]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G63310-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G63310.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64903" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="AAC15253" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="NDK II" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="NDP kinase II" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="NDPK II" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="NDPK Ia" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-34006, RXN-7647, RXN-7646, RXN-6723" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G63310.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G63310" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
